// Let the unprivileged homepanel user start/stop/restart/kill and set limits
// on its own server units (homepanel-server@<id>.service), start the database
// add-on installer, restart phpMyAdmin, start the self-update unit, and
// nothing else.
//
// Only manage-units is granted. For that action systemd passes the unit name
// as a detail, so the rule can be scoped. manage-unit-files (enable/disable)
// gets no unit detail and is deliberately NOT granted; the panel implements
// autostart itself. Requires polkit >= 0.106 (JavaScript rules): Debian 12+,
// Ubuntu 23.10+. See docs/systemd-permissions.md for older hosts.
polkit.addRule(function (action, subject) {
  if (subject.user !== "homepanel") {
    return polkit.Result.NOT_HANDLED;
  }
  if (action.id !== "org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage-units") {
    return polkit.Result.NOT_HANDLED;
  }
  var unit = action.lookup("unit");
  if (unit && unit.indexOf("homepanel-server@") === 0 && unit.indexOf("/") === -1) {
    return polkit.Result.YES;
  }
  // The database add-on (installer + phpMyAdmin) and the owner's
  // self-update button; each is a fixed root unit with no parameters.
  if (unit === "homepanel-database-install.service" || unit === "homepanel-phpmyadmin.service" ||
      unit === "homepanel-update.service") {
    return polkit.Result.YES;
  }
  return polkit.Result.NOT_HANDLED;
});
